  "id": "asenapine",
  "term": "asenapine",
  "definition": "Asenapine is an antipsychotic medicine, notable here as the only one described as FDA-approved in sublingual form. In the supplied source, it is reported to help positive, negative, and depressive symptoms linked with schizophrenia and to have relatively limited metabolic and extrapyramidal side effects compared with some other antipsychotics.",
